    "body": "Refreshed with main (6a10c5ad); the merge itself had no textual conflict. #945 is already in main. Main's recorded-stream guards (#926) arrived with the merge, and this slice's dump writes `PARAM WorkOffset 1.000000` where they had `G54`. So I applied #1113's rule: I regenerated **only** the eight stream files with WRITE_GOLDEN=1 (post `recorded_streams`, app `recorded_post_streams`). Every script golden and posted golden is byte-identical. PROCESS_VERSION is 25, the same as main; this PR doesn't change it. Head 558e61e5.\n\nTests: every camcraft-post suite passes: `work_offset_index` 9, `recorded_streams` 10, all eleven `script_*` suites 9 each, `post_engine` 33, plus the rest. App `sinumerik_work_offsets` 2/2 and `recorded_post_streams` 2/2. Clippy on post and app with `-D warnings` is clean. Mergeable.\n",
